===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|hin}}, from {{etyl|he|en}} {{m|he|הִֽין}}, from {{etyl|egy|en}} {{m|egy|hnw||jar, about half a liter}}: <hiero>h:n-nw-w-W22</hiero>
{{attention|he}}<!--check the Hebrew-->

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An ancient Hebrew unit of liquid measurement, approximately 0.48 [[litre]].
#* Exodus 30:24 (NIV):
#*: 500 shekels of cassia — all according to the sanctuary shekel — and a '''hin''' of olive oil.

